  "body": "## Direct constructive physics\nParent BASS PR162 exact commit `31c41541eb053545f8638177b8e848d5495b57fd`. Preserve original BASS collisionless FD96 mass quadrature, positive angular GL source, Sigma = sqrt(3)|s|/H with separately signed orientation, and PR162 cancellation-resistant DeltaP. Introduce the **analytic susceptibility**:\n```text\nDeltaP = -0.5 \u2202_b rho = \u222b W L/E\n\u2202_b DeltaP = \u222b W [k(-4 e^-4b mu\u00b2 -e^2b(1-mu\u00b2))/E + 2 L\u00b2/E\u00b3]\n\u2202_x rho = -3(rho+pbar),  sigma_ab pi^ab = 2 s DeltaP\n\u2202_b H = -H0\u00b2 (Omega_m fm /a_ref\u00b3) DeltaP / H   [fixed gamma/nu, s,x]\n```\n`jacobian.py` checks the actual BASS Einstein signed-shear ODE partial derivative with finite differences, keeping the native REI whole chemistry Jacobian deliberately unclaimed.\n\n## Executed engineering and science\n- Local Ubuntu Rust 1.99.0 standalone std-only `kernel.rs` actually built and run. **10 new tests PASS**, plus 6 stable / 20 joint / 15 source-evidence / 23 massive original tests rerun, **74 local tests PASS** total.\n- Local Wolfram Language 15.0 + xTensor 1.3.0: 8 exact-zero source-independent GR tensor, susceptibility, pressure derivative and energy/work identities.\n- NCP **s1a0e5abed09** accessed via user-supplied SSH; hardware **64 logical CPUs, 125 GiB RAM**, actual `/root/.cargo/bin/rustc` and Cargo 1.99.0. Source-locked FD96 grids exported from immutable original BASS q/rw, mu/w and energy normalization. Original AX08 159MiB donor and production REI chemistry were NOT copied or modified.\n- **3639 NCP science evaluations**, masses m/Tref=3,30,300 each 1213 cases. All five returned fields (rho,P_perp,P_parallel,DeltaP,dDeltaP/db) **bitwise equal** at widths 1 vs 64; original Python FD96, exact source-input SHA-256, downloaded native TSVs and compiled Rust kernel source independently verified. Cross-language max absolute differences m=3 at most 5.55e-16, m=30 4.44e-16, m=300 8.88e-16.\n- Matched NCP 6000-state, 3-repeat, seven-width *kinetic component only* performance: best m3 32 threads **16.1624x**, m30 64 threads **16.8819x**, m300 64 threads **18.0737x** versus same host single-thread; m3 width64 slower than32. Includes scoped thread launch, excludes I/O and native Einstein/chemistry.\n- Results/provenance/machine receipt under `research/rei_native_stress_ncp_20261015/`: `REPORT_KO.md`, `REI_HANDOFF.json`, `evidence/NCP_VALIDATION_CLEAN.json`, `evidence/NCP_RESULTS/`, `evidence/XACT_JACOBIAN.json`. Checkpoint original failures preserved, and small finite-difference diagnostic refined without widening physics tolerance.\n\n## Scope\n**DERIVED + NUMERICALLY_CHECKED + IMPLEMENTATION_VERIFIED** only for LRS Bianchi I collisionless FD96 massive source/partial Jacobian. The standalone native Rust kernel is not yet adopted by original `rei_microphysics` H/He production driver, does not provide stellar emission/recoil Q^a closure, polarized Thomson, cold full z20\u21924 chemistry, or observables. Current sibling sources REI PR150/152, REI PR145/148/149, BASS_HE PR65, bass_cr PR72 remain separately source-authoritative. An owner-controlled new source schema/checkpoint is required before actual REI production integration.\n\nBackup publishing/restore receipt will be posted separately after completed two-cloud byte readback. No automatic merge.",
